<p>Ref No: {{{Case.Case_Number__c}}}<br />
<br />
Hi {{{Case.First_Name__c}}},<br />
<br />
<b>Baggage Reference - {{{Case.Baggage_File_Reference__c}}}</b></p>

<p>Thank you for contacting the Qantas Customer Care team.<br />
<br />
Before we can help you get your baggage repaired, there are a few things you'll need to do outlined in the steps below.<br />
<br />
<strong>Step 1</strong>: Take your damaged <strong>&lt;baggage/luggage/pram/sporting equipment/surfboard&gt;</strong> to the nearest repairer in your area.<br />
<br />
<strong>Step 2</strong>: Ask for your baggage to be assessed and get a quote for the repair.<br />
<br />
<strong>Step 3</strong>: Send us a copy of the repair quote by replying to this email.<br />
<br />
Additionally, we’ll need to approve the repair before you commence repairs, so please wait for that approval. After all the above are done, we’ll action this as soon as possible.<br />
<br />
If a repair is not possible/feasable, should you&nbsp;have to make a replacement claim please submit your claim via&nbsp;<a href="https://www.qantas.com/en-au/help/contact-us/complaints-feedback-claim-form">Customer care request form | Qantas AU</a>.<br />
<br />
For more information refer to&nbsp;<a href="https://www.qantas.com/en-au/baggage/delayed-lost-damaged">Delayed, lost or damaged baggage | Qantas AU</a></p>
</body>
